{"full":"hf:damigupta/onco_mind","spaceId":"damigupta/onco_mind","name":"OncoMind","source":"huggingface","description":"Cancer Research Copilot - Gap Analysis","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","oncology","cancer","genomics","precision-medicine","bioinformatics","llm","biomedical","genetics","variant-analysis","variant-interpretation","structured-llm","evidence-synthesis","research","streamlit","demo","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":3,"created":"2026-01-14T02:13:28.000Z","updated":"2026-07-29T00:28:49.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"SLEEPING","appUrl":"https://damigupta-onco-mind.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/damigupta/onco_mind","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T15:47:23.946Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T15:47:23.946Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T15:47:23.946Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🚀","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Research intelligence for cancer variants. Find the gaps, not just the facts.","For BRAF V600E, databases already agree. For the next 10,000 variants, the key question is \"what don't we know yet?\"","OncoMind is a research intelligence platform that identifies evidence gaps in cancer variant knowledge—surfacing where research is thin, conflicting, or missing entirely. It's built for translational teams and small biotechs deciding which variants are worth a project, not for treating individual patients."],"features":["Research funding decisions","Clinical trial design","Functional validation studies","Deterministic annotation backbone – structured evidence from knowledge bases, trials, cBioPortal, DepMap, Hotspots, literature","Optional LLM research layer – highlights gaps and drafts hypotheses, constrained by that backbone"],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/damigupta/onco_mind/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"235c5bc9af284609595bd016f9621126a96ac33f6b42e0117c081e0a53241377","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T15:02:07.0